Dynamic linking against an LGPL library is the case the LGPL is written for,
and it imposes no licence on this work. What it asks is that a recipient be
able to substitute their own build of that library, which reading its typelib
at runtime allows even more directly than linking does. The Apache-2.0 terms in
LICENSE therefore cover this gem's own source, and the LGPL covers the library
it calls into.

